  "findings": [
    "Baseline has no terrain-blend material; every art variant activates it. Default-ground-only reproduces114.2s startup/41.6s drive.",
    "Tiles-only has four terrain-blend overlays and loses textured near foreground in viewed captures; faster95.8s startup/6.1s drive is not an acceptable release substitution.",
    "Default ground fallback adds two more terrain overlays; same viewport, six overlays add22242rendered triangles versus baseline. Frame cost is driven by activation/coverage, not number of unique grass assets (one).",
    "Current full candidate160.0s startup/40.5s drive is worse than prior114\u2013119s samples. Additional sky/terrain interaction or frame scheduling remains unresolved; not called baseline noise.",
    "Texture shader creates fixed512atlas and256base mip even for smaller source exports, with nine coverage neighbors and two mip samples plus lookup per neighbor. Source resizing does not remove this rendering path; prior resized experiment failed continuity and remains rejected."
  ],
  "visualReview": "Actual authored Demo before/after drive frames viewed for all four variants. Current day sky and foreground align; no conspicuous sky wrap in sampled straight. Tiles-only exposes flat near-ground fallback and is rejected. No new full245production acceptance; night/fog, extreme pitch and inheritedPevely constraints unchanged. PriorP1images also inspected but desktop-named image is390x844, so it is not counted as desktop proof.",
